From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:16:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: bcm4377: abort suspend if wake IRQ arming fails

With controller wake enabled, bcm4377_suspend() returns success even
when enable_irq_wake() fails. The MSI is then not a wake source, although
HCI has been suspended for remote wake and the function remains in D0.
A fault-injected callback test reproduces a zero return with HCI still
suspended and no wake reference after enable_irq_wake() returns -ENXIO.

Return the arming error and undo HCI suspension using the existing resume
path. Clear the powered-resume epoch before that rollback, since no
system sleep completed, and preserve the original error if HCI rollback
also fails. Arm the IRQ before saving PCI state, so an aborted suspend
does not leave a saved-state marker. The PM core does not invoke resume
for the device whose suspend callback failed.

The extracted PM callbacks pass host tests with mocked kernel APIs for
arming failure, rollback failure, repeated successful wake cycles,
wake-disabled quiescence and HCI suspend failure, with recovery support
on and off. ARM64 kernel build and hardware wake qualification remain
pending; this does not establish the cause of a particular machine hang.

Fixes: 0609ca7fa79a ("Bluetooth: hci_bcm4377: Support remote wakeup")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit d80847118522567a39106da6bc6fb1ba16b57275)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit afd51176986a8ad1f786853a2e44e0f728012c0e)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
index 4a1b595f65..c8b6dbd689 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm4377.c
@@ -2923,6 +2923,8 @@ static int bcm4377_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 					hdev);
 }
 
+static int bcm4377_resume(struct device *dev);
+
 static int bcm4377_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct pci_dev *pdev = to_pci_dev(dev);
@@ -2945,6 +2947,21 @@ static int bcm4377_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	if (device_may_wakeup(dev)) {
+		ret = enable_irq_wake(pdev->irq);
+		if (ret) {
+			int resume_ret;
+
+			dev_err(dev, "Failed to arm Bluetooth wake IRQ: %d\n", ret);
+			/* The PM core will not resume a device that failed suspend. */
+			bcm4377->resume_powered = false;
+			resume_ret = bcm4377_resume(dev);
+			if (resume_ret)
+				dev_err(dev, "Failed to undo Bluetooth suspend: %d\n",
+					resume_ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+		bcm4377->wake_armed = true;
+
 		/*
 		 * Remote wakeup: leave the firmware running and the function
 		 * in D0, so a connection attempt from a wake-allowed device
@@ -2952,7 +2969,6 @@ static int bcm4377_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		 * core from putting the function into D3hot.
 		 */
 		pci_save_state(pdev);
-		bcm4377->wake_armed = !enable_irq_wake(pdev->irq);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
